\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  I'll sing my song to my God and my maker;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The Almighty, my Lord and my Salvation;
\par I give Him Praise for all His works.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  What 'er He likes, He maketh to be stable;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He created all and looks upon all of them;
\par It fades away when He neglects.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  He dwells in light, no evil can be near Him
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He is most high, and rules o'er all creation;
\par His throne exist for evermore.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  He is so rich, and wealth and in comfort,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  in Joy and Peace and in love in aboundance
\par and never short of anything.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Whatever is in Heav'n or on this earth,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He knows them well, and never shall forget them
\par He views them all in one eye sight.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  He is near me, He dwells me by His own side
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 keeps me so safe and make me feel so secured
\par And lays His stronghand upon me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  He stays by me, He search my heart and knows me,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 in all my life, my way and all my movement;
\par He leads me wherever I go.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  8.  When I climb up to Heaven I shall meet Him;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  When I descend to death O, I shall meet Him;
\par   The Lord of Host is everywhere.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  9.   He knows my mind, and my
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  thought cannot hide Him;
\par  He hears my pr'yer, He gracefully
\par  supports me and keeps a safe eye upon me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10.  Whatever I possess is not for me;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Almighty God is the possessor of all,
\par  All that I have belongs to Him.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11.  Omnipotent, your name is wondrous to me
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  I shall never forget to lift up your name
\par   and I shall praise and worship Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12.  Your works are ever wondrous, finest, purest;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0   the sun, the moon, the air and also the strars
\par  proclaim the Power of the Lord.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 13\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 13.   The heav'n and sea the farms, the hills and valeys,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0   the sand and all the mountains surrounded us
\par   reveals and praising all Thy Might.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 14\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 14.  The animals, the trees and all the green leaves
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  the cotton seed and all the little feathers,
\par  reveals your wisdom is so great.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 15\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 15.   You give the rains to water all our green fields,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  and give the yam, the maize, plantain, bananas,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1  \cf0 the fish, the wine and all good drinks.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 16\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   16.   No sparrow nor a little bird shall
\par           ever die and come down, if  Thou stay in us alway;
\par \pard\li315\sl186\slmult0 even thou counteth all my hair.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 17\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   17.  No sorrow shall ever be in my pure heart
\par \pard\li315\sl186\slmult0  that even I can ever be forsaken
\par And Thou have taken all my life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 18\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 18.  I shall never lose any-thing Thou giv'st me;
\par \pard\li315\sl186\slmult0 You are the greatest of all things that I need
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 and Thou alone, art my treasure.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

